TestIdeals -- a package for calculations of singularities in positive characteristic 
*************************************************************************************

Description
===========

TestIdeals is a package for basic computations of $F$-singularities. It is
focused on computing test ideals and related objects. It does this via *note
frobeniusRoot: frobeniusRoot,, which computes $I^{[1/p^e]}$, as introduced by
Blickle-Mustata-Smith (this is equivalent to the image of an ideal under the
Cartier operator in a polynomial ring).

Notable functions:
  * *note testIdeal: testIdeal, computes the test ideal of a normal
    \mathbb{Q}-Gorenstein ring or pair.
  * *note testModule: testModule, computes the parameter test module of a ring
    or pair.
  * *note parameterTestIdeal: parameterTestIdeal, computes the parameter test
    ideal of a Cohen-Macaulay ring.
  * *note FPureModule: FPureModule, computes the stable image of the trace of
    Frobenius on the canonical module.
  * *note isFRegular: isFRegular, checks if a normal \mathbb{Q}-Gorenstein ring
    or pair is $F$-regular.
  * *note isFPure: isFPure, checks if a ring is $F$-pure.
  * *note isFRational: isFRational, checks if a  ring is $F$-rational.
  * *note isFInjective: isFInjective, checks if a  ring is $F$-injective.
  * *note compatibleIdeals: compatibleIdeals, finds the compatibly $F$-split
    ideals with a (near) $F$-splitting.

Consider, for instance, the test ideal of the cone over an elliptic curve.
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/5[x,y,z]/(z*y^2 - x*(x - z)*(x + z));|
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : testIdeal(R)                                |
|                                                 |
|o2 = ideal (z, y, x)                             |
|                                                 |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                  |
+-------------------------------------------------+

The following example was studied by Anurag Singh when showing that
$F$-regularity does not deform.
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : S = ZZ/3[A,B,C,D,T];                             |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : M = matrix{{A^2 + T^4, B, D}, {C, A^2, B^3 - D}};|
|                                                      |
|             2      3                                 |
|o4 : Matrix S  <-- S                                  |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : I = ideal(T) + minors(2, M);                     |
|                                                      |
|o5 : Ideal of S                                       |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : isFRegular(S/I)                                  |
|                                                      |
|o6 = true                                             |
+------------------------------------------------------+


