adicDigit -- compute a digit of the non-terminating expansion of a number in the unit interval in a given base
**************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        d = adicDigit(p, e, x)
        D = adicDigit(p, e, L)
  * Inputs:
      * p, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, greater than 1; the desired
        base
      * e, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, positive, which specifies which
        digit is desired
      * x, a *note rational number: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,, in the interval [0,1];
        the number whose digit is to be computed
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, consisting of rational numbers in
        the interval [0,1] whose digits are to be computed
  * Outputs:
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the e^{th} digit of the base p
        expansion of x
      * D, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, consisting of the e^{th} digits
        of the base p expansions of the elements of L

Description
===========

The command adicDigit(p, e, 0) returns 0. If $x$ is a rational number in the
interval (0,1], then adicDigit(p, e, x) returns the coefficient of $p^{-e}$ in
the non-terminating base $p$ expansion of $x$.

+-------------------------+
|i1 : adicDigit(5, 4, 1/3)|
|                         |
|o1 = 3                   |
+-------------------------+

If $L$ is a list of rational numbers in the unit interval, adicDigit(p, e, L)
returns a list containing the $e^{th}$ digits (base $p$) of the elements of
$L$.

+-------------------------------------+
|i2 : adicDigit(5, 4, {1/3, 1/7, 2/3})|
|                                     |
|o2 = {3, 4, 1}                       |
|                                     |
|o2 : List                            |
+-------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note adicExpansion: adicExpansion, -- compute adic expansion
  * *note adicTruncation: adicTruncation, -- truncation of a non-terminating
    adic expansion

