frobeniusPreimage -- finds the ideal of elements mapped into a given ideal, under all $p^{-e}$-linear maps
**********************************************************************************************************

Description
===========

Given an ideal $Q$ in a ring $R$, one frequently considers $I_e(Q)$.  This is
the ideal of elements $x \in R$ such that $\phi(x^{1/p^e}) \in Q$ for all $\phi
: R^{1/p^e} \to R$.  Sometimes this ideal is called the Frobenius pre-image. In
a regular ring, it agrees with the frobenius power $Q^{[p^e]}$.

+------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/7[x,y,z]/ideal(x*y-z^2);|
+------------------------------------+
|i2 : Q = ideal(x, z);               |
|                                    |
|o2 : Ideal of R                     |
+------------------------------------+
|i3 : frobeniusPreimage(1, Q)        |
|                                    |
|                3    4              |
|o3 = ideal (0, x z, x )             |
|                                    |
|o3 : Ideal of R                     |
+------------------------------------+

In the previous example $I_1(Q)$ agrees with $Q^{(p)}$, the $p$th symbolic
power of $Q$.

Ways to use frobeniusPreimage:
==============================

  * "frobeniusPreimage(ZZ,Ideal)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note frobeniusPreimage: frobeniusPreimage, is a *note method
function with options: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

