parameterTestIdeal -- compute the parameter test ideal of a Cohen-Macaulay ring
*******************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        parameterTestIdeal(R)
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, a Cohen-Macaulay ring
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * FrobeniusRootStrategy => a *note symbol: (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,, default
        value Substitution, selects the strategy for internal frobeniusRoot
        calls
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the parameter test ideal of R

Description
===========

This function computes the parameter test ideal of a Cohen-Macaulay ring $R$.
Technically, it computes \tau($\omega$) : $\omega$ where $\omega$ is a
canonical module of $R$, and \tau($\omega$) is the (parameter) test module, as
computed by *note testModule: testModule,. For example, the ring $R$ in the
following example is $F$-rational, and so its parameter test ideal is the unit
ideal.

+---------------------------------------------+
|i1 : T = ZZ/5[x,y];                          |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i2 : S = ZZ/5[a,b,c,d];                      |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i3 : g = map(T, S, {x^3, x^2*y, x*y^2, y^3});|
|                                             |
|o3 : RingMap T <-- S                         |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i4 : R = S/(ker g);                          |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i5 : parameterTestIdeal(R)                   |
|                                             |
|o5 = ideal 1                                 |
|                                             |
|o5 : Ideal of R                              |
+---------------------------------------------+

Consider now a non-$F$-rational Gorenstein ring, whose test ideal and parameter
test ideal coincide.

+---------------------------------------+
|i6 : R = ZZ/7[x,y,z]/(x^3 + y^3 + z^3);|
+---------------------------------------+
|i7 : parameterTestIdeal(R)             |
|                                       |
|o7 = ideal (z, y, x)                   |
|                                       |
|o7 : Ideal of R                        |
+---------------------------------------+
|i8 : testIdeal(R)                      |
|                                       |
|o8 = ideal (z, y, x)                   |
|                                       |
|o8 : Ideal of R                        |
+---------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note testModule: testModule, -- find the parameter test module of a
    reduced ring
  * *note testIdeal: testIdeal, -- compute a test ideal in a Q-Gorenstein ring

Ways to use parameterTestIdeal:
===============================

  * "parameterTestIdeal(Ring)"

